---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Agentic: an agent that works like you do · inixiative"
  description="Foundry, the workspace around your agent. Kingdom, Archive, Signet, KCP and agent-session: the pieces that keep your agents working the way you do."
  domain="agentic"
  current="agentic"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" data-live></span>Agentic</span>
    <h1 class="display-1">An agent that works like you do.</h1>
    <p class="subhead">Giving your work a voice.</p>
    <p class="lede">
      Every agent session starts half-amnesiac. You pay for it by explaining your conventions, your
      decisions and your taste again. These tools carry what you've already decided into every
      session, and let you decide who and what can reach your work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section anchor-target" id="foundry">
    <div class="card feature" data-raised>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span>Foundry</span>
        <h2 class="display-3">The workspace around your agent.</h2>
        <p>
          Foundry runs on your machine around Claude Code, Codex and Muse, or behind any app that speaks ACP.
          Small expert agents called Wardens notice what your request touches and point your agent at what
          your codebase already has.
        </p>
        <div class="tags">
          <span class="tag" data-tone="open">Source-available · BSL 1.1</span>
        </div>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="/foundry/">How Foundry works</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/inixiative/foundry">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="pitch-list" aria-label="What Foundry does">
        <li>Stop repeating yourself to Claude.</li>
        <li>Every agent you pay for, in one place.</li>
        <li>Stop being a meat proxy. <span class="tag" data-tone="progress">Joiner view in progress</span></li>
        <li>Stop checking a dozen apps. <span class="tag" data-tone="progress">In progress</span></li>
        <li>Set up your repo. <span class="tag" data-tone="progress">In progress</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow" data-quiet>How it works</span>
      <h2>Your machine does the work. Kingdom holds the keys.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Agents run on your computer, on your own subscriptions. Anything that crosses to a teammate or a
        provider goes through Kingdom, on a Signet the owner can take back.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="map">
      <div class="map-node" data-side="yours">
        <span class="eyebrow">Your machine</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Foundry around Claude Code, Codex and Muse</li>
          <li>agent-session runs each session</li>
          <li>Archive keeps every session</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <span class="map-link">Signet</span>
      <div class="map-node">
        <span class="eyebrow">Kingdom</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Who you are, in every team you're in</li>
          <li>Your integrations and their credentials</li>
          <li>Who and what can reach each piece</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <span class="map-link">Signet</span>
      <div class="map-node" data-side="shared">
        <span class="eyebrow" data-side="shared">Shared</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Teammates and their agents</li>
          <li>GitHub, Slack, Linear</li>
          <li>Shared archives</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="legend" aria-label="Colour key">
      <li style="--swatch: var(--app-primary)">yours</li>
      <li style="--swatch: var(--app-tertiary)">shared</li>
      <li style="--swatch: var(--app-quaternary)">Signet</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow" data-quiet>The pieces</span>
      <h2>Use one, or all of them.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <a class="card anchor-target" id="kingdom" href="https://kingdom.inixiative.com">
        <div class="card-head"><h3>Kingdom</h3><span class="tag">Hosted</span></div>
        <p>Everything you're doing, in one place.</p>
        <p class="meta">kingdom.inixiative.com →</p>
      </a>
      <div class="card anchor-target" id="archive">
        <div class="card-head"><h3>Archive</h3><span class="tag" data-tone="open">MIT</span></div>
        <p>Keeps every agent session. Local-first, and it syncs to the archives you choose.</p>
        <div class="card-links"><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/inixiative/archive">GitHub</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card anchor-target" id="signet">
        <div class="card-head"><h3>Signet</h3><span class="tag" data-tone="open">MIT</span></div>
        <p>A revocable pass on the owner's terms. It is how anything uses an integration through Kingdom, with every use tracked and audited.</p>
        <div class="card-links"><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/inixiative/signet">GitHub</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card anchor-target" id="kcp">
        <div class="card-head"><h3>KCP</h3><span class="tags"><span class="tag" data-tone="open">MIT</span><span class="tag" data-tone="progress">In progress</span></span></div>
        <p>Kingdom CLI Proxy. Run your provider CLIs through Kingdom with no credentials on your machine. Kingdom runs the command and streams the output back.</p>
        <div class="card-links"><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/inixiative/kcp">GitHub</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card anchor-target" id="agent-session">
        <div class="card-head"><h3>agent-session</h3><span class="tag" data-tone="open">MIT</span></div>
        <p>Drive Claude Code, Codex and Muse as persistent streaming sessions behind one interface.</p>
        <div class="card-links"><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/inixiative/agent-session">GitHub</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card anchor-target" id="oracle" data-plain>
        <div class="card-head"><h3>Oracle</h3><span class="tag">Closed</span></div>
        <p>Measures whether a correction stuck, and tunes the docs and Wardens.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section anchor-target" id="bench">
    <a class="card" href="https://bench.inixiative.com" data-plain>
      <div class="card-head">
        <span class="eyebrow" data-quiet>bench</span>
        <span class="tag">Results from June 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h3 class="heading-1">Do I Still Have a Job?</h3>
      <p>Our own challenge set for coding agents, from staff to architect level. More challenges are coming.</p>
      <p class="meta">bench.inixiative.com →</p>
    </a>
  </section>
</Base>
